    "answer": "Reviewed the household records, transactions, and unread note and email. **No authorized refund or fee request was supported by the evidence:** the $12 Harbor Bank maintenance fee was reversed, and ShopMart\u2019s $34.10 and $67.92 charges match the two confirmed orders.\n\nI saved two recurring-charge leads: Spotify at $11.99/month and Oakview rent at $2,150/month. I created a waiting approval case asking whether you want Spotify cancelled; I did not change the service. Oakview appears to be consistent rent, with no issue to pursue in the records. Follow-ups are scheduled for October 23.\n\n**Need from you:** confirm whether you want to cancel Spotify. The account directory lists support pages only for Harbor Bank and ShopMart; neither had an unresolved request to submit.\n\nOakview Apartments is closed: the $2,150 charges are consistent monthly rent, with no refund or other amount owed. `review_status` now shows only Spotify still open.\n\nI couldn\u2019t update Spotify\u2019s saved opportunity: finapp returned \u201cRecord not found\u201d when I tried to close it, even though the opportunity appears in work search. The saved waiting case asks whether you want to cancel the $11.99/month service; I made no service change.\n\n`review_status` now reports **done: true** with no remaining items. Spotify\u2019s opportunity is saved as waiting with a blocker: cancelling or changing the $11.99/month service requires your approval. No refund or dispute is supported by the records, so I did not contact Spotify.",
